FreeJ2ME-Plus's core stops the rumble every frame it has none to play, and
calls the frontend's rumble function to do it without checking it has one:
a frontend with no motor (the TrimUI Brick, or Diatom's desktop port) hands
back none, and the first frame without rumble jumped to address 0. The
branch that plays a rumble checks; the one that stops it now does too.

For ZyperOS, mk/build-freej2me.sh applies it; GPL-3.0 as the code it
changes.

--- a/src/libretro/freej2me_libretro.c
+++ b/src/libretro/freej2me_libretro.c
@@ -1103,7 +1103,7 @@
 			rumble.set_rumble_state(0, RETRO_RUMBLE_WEAK,  rumbleStrength);
 			rumbleTime -= 1000 / DEFAULT_FPS;
 		}
-		else
+		else if (rumble.set_rumble_state)
 		{
 			rumble.set_rumble_state(0, RETRO_RUMBLE_STRONG, 0);
 			rumble.set_rumble_state(0, RETRO_RUMBLE_WEAK, 0);
